{{-- Document-owning layout for the uniform marketing pages (features/*,
     for/*), on the proven layouts/status.stx pattern (stx-standards 03).
     NOTE: directive-looking text is LIVE inside these comments (the
     processor scans directives before comment semantics — writing the
     extends directive with its own name here made the layout extend
     ITSELF and OOM). Pages extend layouts/marketing and fill ONE
     section — content (the page's <main> interior, verbatim). SEO
     (title/description/canonical/og/twitter/JSON-LD) is declared in each
     page's server script via useSeoMeta + useHead; the framework
     renders it into this head server-side
     charset/viewport live here (a document-owning layout writes its own;
     the config app.head pair is fragment-only). Favicons + fonts come
     from config/ui.ts app.head via injectConfigHeadTags. The index,
     compare, docs, login and register pages are NOT on this layout yet -
     they differ structurally and convert individually (see
     STX-MIGRATION-PLAN.md Phase 2). --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-theme="system">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    {{-- Title/description/canonical/og/twitter come from each page's
         useSeoMeta + useHead calls (stx-standards 04) — the framework
         splices them into this head server-side. --}}
    @include('../partials/marketing-head.stx')
  </head>
  <body>
    @include('../partials/marketing-nav.stx')

    <main>
@yield('content')
    </main>

    @include('../partials/marketing-footer.stx')
  </body>
</html>
